{"text": "From:\nDate:\nSubject:\nTo:\n\nce:\n\n2071037425 Page 1\nNote for Keane, Denise\n\nPoole, Jay rue\nFri, Jan 19, 1996 3:19 PM\nKY Senate Bill\n\nSlavitt, Josh\n\nCrawford, Derek; Keane, Denise; Liebengood, Howard; Merlo, Ellen;\n\u2018coli, David; Walls, Tina\n\nUnder the leadership of Kentucky Farm Bureau, Senate Bill 137 was introduced yesterday.\nAmong the patrons are the Senate President and the Chairman of the Tobacco Task Force. It\nhas the blessing of most of the grower community and retail community. \u2018The bill as,\nintroduced contains the following new provisions:\n\n1. Picture ID proof of age\n2. Raises fines for selling to minors from $10 for first offense to $100 for first offense.\nSubsequent fines are also raised.\n3. Makes it unlawful for minors to purchase cigarettes. First offense subjects said minor to\n$50 fine and 20 hours of community service.\n4, Raises penalty for providing samples to minors from $100 for first offense to $1000 for\nfirst offense.\n5. Requires line of sight at retail.\n6. Store owners would be required by law to notify each employee to secure proof of age\n\u2018when the prospective purchaser appears to be under the age of 18.\n\nAll fines are to be enforced by the Department of Agriculture using existing Civil enforcement\nprocedures, One-tenth of one cent of the current 3 cent state tobacco tax will be used to\ncreate enforcement funding,\n\nWell send up under separate cover the specific language. Please don't hesitate to call me or\nDan Ison if you have any questions.",
